WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.252
A custom task extension carries the part
of a leaver the built-in tasks don't,

3
00:00:06.252 --> 00:00:09.513
so its evidence is account
and credential removal.

4
00:00:09.513 --> 00:00:14.813
A callback that reports what really happened,
at once, with one effect per delivery,

5
00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:19.881
supports NIST special publication eight
hundred fifty-three controls A C two,

6
00:00:19.881 --> 00:00:23.467
account management, and P S
four, personnel termination;

7
00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.274
the evidence is the
task processing result.

8
00:00:26.274 --> 00:00:30.024
The definition passing lint,
with long retries refused,

9
00:00:30.024 --> 00:00:32.387
leaves the pull request's check run.

10
00:00:32.387 --> 00:00:36.851
Building from the reviewed registry,
with shared access signatures off and

11
00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:41.101
proof-of-possession on, leaves the
repository and the deployment record.

12
00:00:41.101 --> 00:00:45.750
The read-back checks, and the leaver
blocking first, are filed with the change.

13
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.187
The extension's authorized apps show the

14
00:00:48.187 --> 00:00:51.125
callback identity has no
tenant-wide permission.

15
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:55.763
And in Lab 2, an on-demand run
leaves the Logic App's run history.

16
00:00:55.763 --> 00:00:59.375
The KSI column is FedRAMP's
Key Security Indicators,

17
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:02.651
the FedRAMP 20x indicators for providers.

18
00:01:02.651 --> 00:01:06.260
Which output supports which
control is this workbook's reading.
